WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.175
Clinical trials decide who can join with a long list of rules.

00:00:04.175 --> 00:00:07.791
Thirty, forty of them… written for doctors, not for patients.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.227
So here's a made-up patient.

00:00:10.227 --> 00:00:15.664
She's fifty-two, her breast cancer has spread, and she lives in Honolulu.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.526
Then a line in her own words: ER-positive, HER2-negative… no treatment yet.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.528
And none of this gets stored.

00:00:26.528 --> 00:00:28.969
It stays in her browser tab.

00:00:29.319 --> 00:00:31.524
TrialScout asks ClinicalTrials.

00:00:31.524 --> 00:00:37.214
gov what's recruiting nearby… then checks her against every rule, one at a time.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.719
Seventeen trials within a hundred kilometers.

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:47.619
For eight of them, nothing likely rules her out.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.548
Each card adds it up: the rules she likely meets… and the ones only her doctor can answer.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.506
The trials where something likely rules her out?

00:01:05.506 --> 00:01:07.113
They go to the bottom.

00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:10.034
Not hidden… because the AI can be wrong.

00:01:10.384 --> 00:01:11.561
Let's open this one.

00:01:11.561 --> 00:01:15.678
Every answer sits right next to the trial's own words, quoted exactly.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.226
Advanced, ER-positive, HER2-negative… likely meets.

00:01:21.576 --> 00:01:25.249
And when it doesn't know enough, it doesn't guess.

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:29.657
It says: ask your doctor… and gives her the question to ask.

00:01:30.007 --> 00:01:34.279
She can print those questions and take them to her next appointment.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.873
Every trial links back to its official page, so this is where the conversation starts… not where it ends.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.017
TrialScout is a prototype.

00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:50.878
It's not medical advice.

00:01:50.878 --> 00:01:54.059
The rule checks come from TypeSafe's Jev.
